      "description": "Lifters raise the bauxite and drop it, so lumps rub and impact each other in water. Fine clay (often rich in reactive silica, which costs caustic soda in digestion) is washed off and leaves with the trommel undersize. Drum speed is typically ~ 50–75 % of critical speed.",
